---
source: crates/e2e/tests/proton.rs
expression: w.transcript()
---
######## 

(human) $ kagebunshin unlock
Passphrase for the local store: 
unlocked

$ kagebunshin project init web
created project web with environment dev

-- before Proton Pass is connected

$ kagebunshin list --provider proton
kagebunshin: cannot list proton: proton: credentials are missing or expired
hint: run `kagebunshin connect proton`
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin project add-source web dev --provider proton --prefix web/
added a source to environment dev of project web; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment dev of project web: Proton Pass: credentials missing or expired (1 source, checked <time> UTC)
ask the human: run `kagebunshin connect proton`
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin next
the environment cannot be resolved
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `kagebunshin connect proton` in a terminal, so kagebunshin can read proton (personal access token).
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

-- the human connects it: first with a token Proton refuses

(human) $ KAGEBUNSHIN_PROTON_TOKEN=$(cat $T/old-token) kagebunshin connect proton --expires 2099-01-31
Passphrase for the local store: 
checking the token with pass-cli, through the daemon
kagebunshin: Proton refused the token
hint: check the token, or create a new personal access token in Proton Pass and run `kagebunshin connect proton` again
[exit 1]

(human) $ KAGEBUNSHIN_PROTON_TOKEN=$(cat $T/token) kagebunshin connect proton --expires 2099-01-31
Passphrase for the local store: 
checking the token with pass-cli, through the daemon
connected Proton Pass: the token reads 2 vaults; it is saved in the local store

$ kagebunshin status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  proton  personal access token  ok
project: web
env: dev
.env.example: none found
2 keys
  DATABASE_URL  proton:web/DATABASE_URL
  STRIPE_KEY    proton:web/STRIPE_KEY

$ kagebunshin list --provider proton
3 matches
  global/OPENAI_KEY  item i4  proton  OPENAI_KEY
  web/DATABASE_URL   item i1  proton  DATABASE_URL
  web/STRIPE_KEY     item i2  proton  STRIPE_KEY

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo database is ${DATABASE_URL:+set}, stripe is ${STRIPE_KEY:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (2 keys); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
database is set, stripe is set

-- one key from the shared vault, under another name

$ kagebunshin project add-source web dev --provider proton --secret global/OPENAI_KEY --key OPENAI_API_KEY
added a source to environment dev of project web

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo openai is ${OPENAI_API_KEY:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (3 keys); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
openai is set

-- the two-hour session ends: kagebunshin logs in again by itself

$ kagebunshin sync
web dev: 3 keys

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo database is ${DATABASE_URL:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (3 keys); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
database is set

-- the token is revoked in Proton

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo database is ${DATABASE_URL:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (3 keys); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
database is set

$ kagebunshin sync
web dev: failed: cannot resolve environment dev of project web: Proton Pass: credentials missing or expired (2 sources, checked <time> UTC)
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment dev of project web: Proton Pass: credentials missing or expired (2 sources, checked <time> UTC)
ask the human: Proton refused the saved token (expired or revoked?): create a new personal access token and run `kagebunshin connect proton`
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment dev of project web: Proton Pass: credentials missing or expired (2 sources, checked <time> UTC)
ask the human: Proton refused the saved token (expired or revoked?): create a new personal access token and run `kagebunshin connect proton`
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin status
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment dev of project web: Proton Pass: credentials missing or expired (2 sources, checked <time> UTC)
ask the human: Proton refused the saved token (expired or revoked?): create a new personal access token and run `kagebunshin connect proton`
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin next
